{"name":"Mud Room","hex":"#60584b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mud room","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of mudroom."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mud_room"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vestibule (architecture)","blocks":[{"text":"A vestibule is a small room leading into a larger space such as a lobby, entrance hall, or passage, for the purpose of waiting, withholding the larger space from view, reducing heat loss, providing storage space for outdoor clothing (mudroom), etc. The term applies to structures in both modern and classical architecture since ancient times."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Arch-render-vestibule.png/330px-Arch-render-vestibule.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vestibule_(architecture)","wikidata":"Q301276"},{"title":"Mud","blocks":[{"text":"Mud is loam, silt, or clay mixed with water. Mud is usually formed after rainfall or near water sources. Ancient mud deposits hardened over geological time to form sedimentary rock such as shale or mudstone. When geological deposits of mud are formed in estuaries, the resultant layers are termed bay muds. Mud has also been used for centuries as a construction resource, mostly for houses, and also as a binder. An Old English word for it was fen, now in most dialects referring to a type of wetland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/2003-11-27_Northerner_boots_in_mud.jpg/330px-2003-11-27_Northerner_boots_in_mud.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mud","wikidata":"Q170449"},{"title":"Room","blocks":[{"text":"In a building or a ship, a room is any enclosed space within a structure, typically bounded by walls to which entry is possible only via a door or other dividing structure. The entrance connects it to either a passageway, another room, or the outdoors. The space is typically large enough for several people to move about. The size, fixtures, furnishings, and sometimes placement of the room within the building or ship support the activity to be conducted in it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Ateneul_Rom%C3%A2n_-_Sala.jpg/330px-Ateneul_Rom%C3%A2n_-_Sala.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Room","wikidata":"Q180516"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Windfang%2C_Bad_Kissingen%2C_Obere_Saline%2C_2014.jpg/500px-Windfang%2C_Bad_Kissingen%2C_Obere_Saline%2C_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Windfang%2C_Bad_Kissingen%2C_Obere_Saline%2C_2014.jpg/1280px-Windfang%2C_Bad_Kissingen%2C_Obere_Saline%2C_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Windfang%2C_Bad_Kissingen%2C_Obere_Saline%2C_2014.jpg/500px-Windfang%2C_Bad_Kissingen%2C_Obere_Saline%2C_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vestibule in Germany.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWindfang%2C_Bad_Kissingen%2C_Obere_Saline%2C_2014.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Croatia-01239_-_The_Peristil_%289551533404%29.jpg/500px-Croatia-01239_-_The_Peristil_%289551533404%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Croatia-01239_-_The_Peristil_%289551533404%29.jpg/1280px-Croatia-01239_-_The_Peristil_%289551533404%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Croatia-01239_-_The_Peristil_%28955153